From: roc-native-macos engine patch series
Subject: [PATCH 0002] Mount each static node kind in a function of its own
Upstream: not yet sent (proposed in https://github.com/lukewilliamboswell/roc-signals/issues/306)
Applies to: roc-signals a13ff70e + 0001, platform/Core.roc

What
  Move the bodies of `mount_elem`'s `Element`, `Comment`, `Text` and
  `TextV` branches into `mount_element`, `mount_comment`, `mount_text` and
  `mount_text_v`, which `mount_elem` calls. `mount_element` recurses into
  `mount_elem` for the children exactly as the branch did. Nothing else
  changes: same commands, same order, same block contents.

Why
  With 0001 applied, a block holding many dynamic sites (a grid of
  `Engine.state` cells) still mounted quadratically: the block's child
  lists (`children`, 240-byte instances; `child_reads`; `child_top`) had
  refcount 2 when `add_child` appended to them (lldb watchpoint on the
  copy's refcount: an incref inside `mount_elem` just before the append,
  then `reallocate` copies), so each site copied every earlier sibling.
  The extra reference is the compiler's; with the static branches out of
  `mount_elem` the block stays unique. Neither moving the `Element` branch
  alone nor the text branches alone was enough, and this patch without
  0001 changes nothing (it depends on 0001). Same compiler caveat as 0001.

Measured (as 0001; before = with 0001 applied)
  Engine.state cells:    1024    2500    4900
    before               16.7    74.2   320.5
    after                 6.7    14.8    28.1
  grid bench, mount engine ms:
                         N=32    N=100
    before               33.0   2360.4
    after                10.2     74.4
  Against the pristine engine (0001 + 0002): N=32 71.0 -> 10.2 ms,
  N=100 17476 -> 74.4 ms, now linear (about 7 us per hover cell).
  Turns are unchanged (N=100 hover p50 2.4 ms, timer p50 1.2 ms).
  With nightly-2026-11-14 (roc-stable) the state-cell mount goes from
  48.2 / 236.4 / 1941.0 ms to 14.2 / 32.7 / 62.8 ms.

